            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "bmc/firmware-handler/test/file_handler_unittest.cpp",
                    "line": 94,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brandon Kim",
                        "email": "brandonkim@google.com",
                        "username": "brandonkimbk"
                    },
                    "message": "I believe we can either do:\n\n`EXPECT_THAT(result, testing::Optional(testPattern));`\n```suggestion\n    EXPECT_THAT(result, testing::Optional(testPattern));\n```\n\nOr `EXPECT_EQ(result.value(), testPattern);` which gracefully handles optional being empty case"
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc/firmware-handler/test/file_handler_unittest.cpp",
                    "line": 94,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jayanth Othayoth",
                        "email": "ojayanth@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ojayanth"
                    },
                    "message": "I tried this and not working as expected . clang-tidy\u2019s bugprone-unchecked-optional-access only accepts a plain C++ guard (e.g., if (!result) return;) before dereferencing std::optional. Test macros (ASSERT_TRUE, EXPECT_THAT(Optional(...))) aren\u2019t modeled by the analyzer, so they don\u2019t silence the warning."
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc/firmware-handler/test/file_handler_unittest.cpp",
                    "line": 94,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brandon Kim",
                        "email": "brandonkim@google.com",
                        "username": "brandonkimbk"
                    },
                    "message": "Hmm.. ok - maybe the clang-tidy has changed since I last wrote a test with optional"
                }
            ],
